  "id": "theatre",
  "kind": "building",
  "notes": "Theatre (11×14, D-054): a Roman theatre in warm stone — a half-round cavea of six tiers of seats rising toward the back (-y) with radial stairways, ringed by a two-storey arcaded outer wall with a cornice; the round orchestra floor in front of a stone stage with a timber floor and niches; the tall scaenae frons with three doors and two storeys of columns under a lean-to tiled roof, side wings with tiled roofs and flags, and the stage house behind; toward the road a colonnaded garden court (porticus) with tiled portico roofs, a fountain, two statues and cypresses, entered through a gate of two piers with a lintel. Service building: no cart, chimney or smoke.",
